{"cause":"B1 completed containment reports could carry a caller-supplied reference without a mandatory trusted authority verification seam, so CF3/CF4 needed to reject unverified terminal reports before accepting output or evidence.","cause_status":"known","event_id":"e1d4a2c7-8a1f-4c29-b4e7-0d5a6f91c3b2","event_sha256":"4f5b46b5685ef5f2717cd93b5ff18fca761c0f2ef82516072e0e5777398c122b","evidence":{"kind":"focused_regression","observed_at":"2026-07-27T18:10:00.000Z","ref":"390 focused tests passed; frontend npx tsc --noEmit passed; diff sha before commit 00823164ae9c1d33735e5c43d06619d49b3bd1408a4e0b438b7f6f33d3171b0a","sha256":"00823164ae9c1d33735e5c43d06619d49b3bd1408a4e0b438b7f6f33d3171b0a"},"impact":"Terminal CF3 validation and CF4 model.custom execution now require an explicit trusted report verifier; the absence of that authority leaves execution unavailable rather than accepting a self-asserted containment result.","incident_id":"e1d4a2c7-8a1f-4c29-b4e7-0d5a6f91c3b2","lesson":"Bind native containment output to a trusted authority verification reference before it enters statistical evidence, Artifact completion, Notebook state, or active-head progression.","lesson_key":"containment-report-authority-boundary","links":["backend/workbench/native_containment/broker.py","backend/workbench/native_containment/contracts.py","backend/workbench/capability_factory/validation_runner.py","backend/workbench/capability_factory/custom_dispatcher.py","backend/workbench/capability_factory/notebook_bridge.py","tests/test_native_containment_broker.py"],"prev_event_sha256":"0607ff7e89dd805b9e7a78db64b68a40d3acecd52deebbf72fc006c951c78dc9","preventability":"preventable","resolution":"resolved","schema_version":1,"severity":"high","stage":"review","subtype":"containment_report_authority_verification_bound","timestamp":"2026-07-27T18:10:00.000Z","type":"REVIEW"}
